 This install applies to "Pokeri", an unofficial Amiga port of the Finnish
 RAY video poker game. Amiga port by Vesa Halttunen / Vesuri.


 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad version 17.0 or better and a PAL Amiga with a
 68020 or better. An A1200 with Fast RAM is recommended; AGA is not required.
 The installed program reserves 1024 KB ChipMem and 4608 KB OtherMem
 including its Kickstart image. Allow additional memory for the host system,
  WHDLoad and PRELOAD. Installation needs Installer V43 or later and 2 MB
 disk space.

 The game also requires a Kickstart 3.1 image and matching relocation file in
 "Devs:Kickstarts" or "WHDCOMMON:". Supported pairs are:

   kick40063.A600  and kick40063.A600.RTB
   kick40068.A1200 and kick40068.A1200.RTB
   kick40068.A4000 and kick40068.A4000.RTB

 These filenames do not require a particular Amiga model. The relocation files
 are available in the Aminet archive "util/boot/skick346.lha". Neither the
 Kickstart images nor the original game ROMs are included in this package.


 Installation:
 -------------
 Supply one drawer containing these four original ROM files, each exactly
 65536 bytes, with no filename extension:

   77POK30   77POK38   77POK34   PARA200J

 Run the Install icon and select the destination. The installer defaults to
 Intermediate experience level. If a Pokeri drawer exists, choose whether to
 remove it first; removing it also removes saved credits and accounting.
 Keeping it preserves ROMs and saves while updating the program.

 If all four ROMs are already installed, their location is not asked again.
 Otherwise, select the drawer containing the four unpacked files. Do not
 select a ZIP archive. Other ROM revisions are not supported.

 Start the game using its Pokeri icon. PRELOAD is enabled by default;
 disable that Tooltype if there is insufficient memory to cache the files.
 Keep the NoVBRMove and NoWriteCache Tooltypes enabled. Both are required for
 this port to run and save reliably under WHDLoad.

 To start from a Shell in the installed drawer:

   WHDLoad Pokeri.slave PRELOAD NOVBRMOVE NOWRITECACHE

 Quitting and saving:
 --------------------
 Escape or the left mouse button quits normally and saves machine state and
 credits. Always quit this way to save changes, rather than resetting.
 WHDLoad's external QuitKey is unavailable with NoVBRMove enabled.

 The files nvram.bin and accounting.bin are created automatically in the data
 drawer under WHDLoad. Keep both to retain the machine state, and keep the
 drawer writable. Previous saves are kept as nvram.bak and accounting.bak.
 To restore a backup, quit the game and copy the .bak file over its .bin file.
 A fresh installation initializes itself and starts with zero credits.


 Features:
 ---------
 - original Finnish video poker game, including holding cards and doubling
 - Amiga graphics, music and sound effects
 - saved credits and accounting, restored on subsequent launches

 Startup and some animations can be slow; sound changes may be delayed
 during heavy drawing.


 Controls:
 ---------
 C               insert coin
 Space           deal / draw
 1 through 5     hold the corresponding card
 D               double a winning hand
 Left / Right    big / small when doubling
 Escape          quit and save
 Left mouse      quit and save
 F1              service door
 F2              operator control
 F3              lamp panel

 If using an emulator, set port 0 to Mouse and port 1 to Nothing. Keyboard
 joystick emulation may otherwise consume the cursor keys.


